# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# tsbuildinfo is incremental-compile state, never shipped.
*.tsbuildinfo
#
# dist/ IS NOT COMMITTED ( ruled 2026-08-13, reversing the 2026-07-23 alpha ruling ).
#
# It was committed so a standalone clone ran with no build step. The cost was a committed artifact
# whose provenance ran through kcd_sdk's OWN dist/ — which is gitignored — so the shipped bundle
# encoded a source state that existed in no commit anywhere: whoever last built decided what shipped
# and nothing recorded what their tree looked like. A build output that can silently disagree with the
# source beside it is the drift cause, not the convenience.
#
# What replaces it: esbuild now bundles kcd_sdk from SOURCE ( one hop, see build.js ), and `prepare`
# runs the build on `npm install`. A clone is still one command — it is `npm install` instead of
# `npm run build`, and it cannot be forgotten or go stale.
#
# Packing does NOT read this file: .npmignore exists solely to stop npm's .gitignore fallback, and
# package.json's `files` array is the allowlist for what ships. dist/ ships; it just is not tracked.
dist/
# build.js and run.js are SOURCE ( repo root ), not output.

# ── Logs & debug artifacts ────────────────────────────────────
*.log
startup.log

# ── Environment & secrets ─────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── OS / editor cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
npm-debug.log*
